# Phase 3
# Captured 2026-07-28 on Jetson Orin Nano Dev Kit (JetPack 6 / L4T R36.4.7,
# qemu-system-aarch64 6.2.0, host kernel 5.15.148-tegra).
#
# Command:
#   sudo qemu-system-aarch64 -machine virt,gic-version=3 -accel tcg -cpu max \
#     -smp 2 -m 1G -drive file=disk-qemu,if=none,id=drv0,format=raw \
#     -device virtio-blk-device,drive=drv0 -kernel ifs.bin -nographic \
#     -serial file:boot-tcg.log -display none -no-reboot -monitor none
#
# Same output/ifs.bin + output/disk-qemu as the cloud-twin Phase-1 build
# (com.qnx.qnx800.target.qemuvirt, mkqnximage --type=qemu --arch=aarch64le).
# This is a CONTROL run under pure software emulation (-accel tcg), used to
# isolate a KVM-specific hang (see docs/orin-port.md risk register,
# "KVM boot hangs silently after FOUND GICv3 ITS" row, 2026-07-28 entry).
# This log proves the IFS/disk pair itself boots correctly on real Orin
# Nano hardware when KVM acceleration is not in the loop.
#
# Honest framing: this is NOT a KVM boot. It does not exercise real
# hardware-backed vGICv3, and it is not the Phase-3 success criterion
# (that requires -enable-kvm per docs/orin-port.md). It is diagnostic
# evidence only.

